  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are tasked with designing a backup and recovery solution for a high-priority application running on Google Cloud Platform. The application uses Cloud Bigtable and Cloud SQL (MySQL) as its primary data stores. Which of the following backup and recovery strategies would best meet the requirements for minimizing data loss and ensuring quick recovery in case of a disaster, while also providing a cost-effective solution?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Enable automated backups for both Cloud Bigtable and Cloud SQL, and use Cloud Storage for storing backups.<br/>B. Use Cloud Storage Transfer Service to create daily snapshots of Cloud Bigtable and Cloud SQL instances.<br/>C. Configure regional replication for Cloud Bigtable instances and use Cloud Functions to periodically export data from Cloud SQL to Cloud Storage.<br/>D. Use Cloud Bigtable's scheduled snapshots for backups and enable Point-in-Time Recovery for Cloud SQL.",
